        "blast_url": "https://blast.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/Blast.cgi?PAGE_TYPE=BlastSearch&PROG_DEF=blastn&BLAST_SPEC=GDH_GCA_937001455.1",
        "comments": "The assembly mOrcOrc1.1 is based on 34x PacBio data generated by the Darwin Tree of Life Project (https://www.darwintreeoflife.org/) and Hi-C data made publicly available by DNA Zoo (https://dnazoo.org); PMID:28336562. The assembly process included the following sequence of steps: initial PacBio assembly generation with Hifiasm, retained haplotig separation with purge_dups, and Hi-C based scaffolding with YaHS. The mitochondrial genome was assembled using MitoHiFi. Finally, the assembly was analysed and manually improved using rapid curation. Chromosome-scale scaffolds confirmed by the Hi-C data have been named in order of size. Order and orientation of scaffolds in a repetitive region of chromosome 17 (\n33.6Mb) is uncertain.",
